 Electron chooses typed shell copy in the eight [shipped Client languages](../../packages/client/locale/README.md) from its application locale and falls back to English. The macOS application bundle declares all eight languages in `CFBundleLocalizations`, allowing macOS to match the initial application language to the user’s preferred languages. Saved Client UI language preferences still take precedence for the main interface. Windows NSIS installer resources live in one JSON file per language under `installer/locales/`; packaging generates NSIS strings and discovers the installer language list from these files. All shipped language resources must have matching keys, format placeholders, and command examples; `pnpm run check:i18n` validates them. The native installer test builds and exercises each configured language. Platform account pages and onboarding artwork use English for languages other than Chinese. On Windows, the main document's language updates desktop menus, recovery and update prompts. The repository Client UI i18n gate checks desktop sources.
 
-Desktop packaging copies `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` into the build-only `DSH_DESKTOP_PRODUCT_NAME` before the official client build resolves its own title, and seals the product name into the About panel and localized shell copy, including native menus and recovery prompts; it defaults to DeepSeek Harness. Electron may retain an internal package identifier in `app.name`, so shell copy does not use that value as the product brand. Branding does not change Electron's application name or user-data directory, and model-provider names remain unchanged.
+Desktop packaging copies `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` into the build-only `DSH_DESKTOP_PRODUCT_NAME` before the official client build resolves its own title, and seals the product name into the About panel and localized shell copy, including native menus and recovery prompts; it defaults to DeepSeek Harness. Electron may retain an internal package identifier in `app.name`, so shell copy does not use that value as the product brand. Official branding keeps Electron's application name and user-data directory unchanged; the AgentKit Studio product overrides that internal name to `agentkit-studio-desktop` so it owns its single-instance lock, user-data directory, and plugin profile, while sessions, credentials, and workspaces remain in the shared DSH home. Model-provider names remain unchanged.
 
 Windows and macOS relay native fullscreen transitions and the state after each page load to the renderer, so overlays can adapt their caption clearance.
 
